<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muslim conquest of the Maghreb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">647–709</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Arab conquest of North Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muslim conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> was the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> and Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a> between 647 and 709. Early raids were followed by the founding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a> in about 670, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> resistance under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a> and the queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dihya">Dihya</a> and the Byzantine hold on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> slowed the advance. Carthage fell in 698, and by 709 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> had reached the Atlantic, preparing the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in 711.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-maghreb.jpg" alt="Muslim conquest of the Maghreb" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Husein Mu'nis et al. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%81%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%AD_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%BA%D8%B1%D8%A8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
